{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "30", "m": "07", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "03", "S": "52"}}, "news": [{"title": "Lucknow: LDA makes fire safety certificates mandatory for building map approval", "para": "Building map approvals in Lucknow now require mandatory fire safety certificates.  Commercial and public-use buildings must submit a valid fire NOC before approval.  Smaller buildings will submit affidavits and undergo audits within three months.  This new rule applies to various establishments like hotels and schools.  The LDA aims to enhance fire safety before construction commences.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/lucknow-development-authority-enforces-mandatory-fire-safety-certificates-for-building-approvals/132732001?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-518482/132732001.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Construction waste plant in Gurugram faces heat over approval, tree-felling charges", "para": "Residents near a proposed construction waste plant in Gurgaon reported tree felling.  The Haryana Pollution Control Board has not received any plant proposal.  Local authorities awarded a contract for boundary fencing and a waste dump site.  Residents have filed a complaint seeking an investigation into alleged violations.  Concerns persist regarding health impacts and adherence to environmental laws.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/controversy-surrounds-gurugram-construction-waste-plant-over-tree-felling-and-approval-issues/132731911?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1655877/132731911.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Delhi civic body demolishes 14 unauthorised properties, seals one", "para": "The Municipal Corporation of Delhi demolished fourteen unauthorized properties and sealed one more.  Civic officials also issued sixteen show-cause notices for illegal construction activities.  This action is part of an ongoing citywide enforcement drive against building norm violations.  Since June first, the civic body has demolished 681 properties.  Residents are urged to obtain necessary approvals before undertaking any construction work.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/mcd-demolishes-14-illegal-properties-in-major-crackdown/132731855?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-223622/132731855.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}